From f6c2a383eb29abcd0362fb7230b1735d17f42264 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Muse=20=28=C3=86THERGENESIS=20review=29?= <review@localhost>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 05:13:38 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Week 2 fixes: 5 simulation-correctness bugs (PH1, PH4, M1-M3)

PH1: n-body no longer discards ~57% of cosmic-mode time. MAX_SUBSTEPS 64->160
covers a full 0.3 yr tick (150 substeps at 0.002 yr); accumulator-cap drops are
now logged, not silent.
PH4: red-giant visuals use authoritative StellarPhysics radius (up to 100x)
instead of the rederived 6x-linear approximation; removed dead getCurrentLum
(6x vs physics 100x luminosity curve); shared WORLD_UNITS_PER_R_SUN constant.
M1: white-dwarf remnant mass clamped to progenitor mass (0.3 Msun progenitor
no longer yields a 0.5 Msun remnant).
M2: remnant visual boundaries aligned with physics: BH branch >= 15 (was >),
pulsar branch > 8 (was >=) so exact 15.0/8.0 Msun match computeRemnantType.
M3: WS sim-state payload reports phase-aware currentMass/currentRadius from
the star's authoritative StellarPhysics state instead of MS formulas.
